# Tokens in components (`@refineui/react`)

Color, padding, spacing, radius, motion, and dimensions come from `@refineui/tokens` and component token maps — never from ad-hoc literals.

See `design-system` rule for package layout.

## MUST
- **Color·spacing·radius·stroke·typography·shadow·z-index·motion** come only from `@refineui/tokens` or resolved component token refs.
- **Foundation size scale** is referenced via **`foundationSizes`** / CSS `--refineui-size-foundation-size-*`.
- **Component dimensions** come only from **`componentSizes`** (aliases of foundationSizes). **Icon glyphs** use **`iconSizes`**; modal scrim uses **`overlays`**.
- **No hardcoding**: no arbitrary `px`, `#hex`, or `rgb()` in component styles. (Exceptions: literal `0`, `minWidth: 0`.)
- When new dimensions are needed, extend `foundationSizes` then `componentSizes` in `packages/tokens` first.

## RECOMMENDED
- Documentation previews use the same tokens and semantic alias utilities (`bg-refineui-alias-*`, `text-refineui-alias-*`).